  "goodToKnow": "Die Studiengebühr is a tuition fee, mostly used in the plural. After a 2005 court ruling, seven western states introduced general fees of about 500 euros a semester, but protests led all of them to abolish them again by 2014. Since 2017, Baden-Württemberg charges most non-EU students 1,500 euros per semester. All students pay a Semesterbeitrag, which usually includes a transport ticket. Plural: die Studiengebühren."
